From 9566f0bcc6efba1e68c0a6ab3e2e50effef68a2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 10:52:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 69/73] fix(reaper): self-heal orphaned wisp_dependencies
 (dangling parent refs)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wisp compaction/purge deletes wisps without cascade-deleting their reverse
wisp_dependencies rows; batchDeleteRows only reverse-deletes edges for parents
purged in the SAME run, so pre-existing/compaction-created orphans were never
removable. The reaper re-flagged them as dangling_parent_ref every scan and
HIGH-escalated the same non-impacting condition forever (20+ times during a
14h e-stop), drowning real alerts.

Add reaper.Repair(): batch-deletes wisp_dependencies rows whose declared internal
parent (wisp via depends_on_wisp_id OR issue via depends_on_issue_id) exists in
neither table, mirroring Scan's dangling detection but as a superset (also cleans
orphaned 'blocks' edges). Batched by primary key (multi-table DELETE can't LIMIT),
autocommit-off + COMMIT + DOLT_COMMIT like Purge. Wired into the daemon reaper
cycle (self-heals automatically → scan stays clean → no escalation spam), the
`gt reaper run` full cycle, and a new `gt reaper repair` subcommand (--dry-run,
--json). TestRepairMatchesDanglingDetection guards against repair/detection drift
(which would loop the anomaly forever).

Validated live: injected synthetic orphan -> scan count=1 -> gt reaper repair
deleted=1 -> scan clean. Data backfill already cleared 854 pre-existing orphans
(hq 395, feryn 459); both DBs now scan anomalies=null.

Closes hq-6f1x, hq-c074.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
